  "result": "The gate returned **OK** for NRS_484D_165_4 on the first run, so 5 of the 6 runs are left. It checked 6 witnesses, the rule uses 3 names, and it composes no other rule.\n\n**Rule** (`library/TrafficSpec/Rules/NRS_484D/NRS_484D_165_4.lean`):\n- **Who it covers:** the subject must be a member of the vehicle aggregate (`DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle`).\n- **When it applies:** the vehicle is parked (`drv_motion_parked`, using `p.halt_speed_tolerance` and `p.parking_min_duration`) and its headlamps are lit, meaning on low beam or high beam.\n- **The duty:** the headlamps are on low beam.\n\nThe node's record spelled out every span, so I made no reading choices of my own and declared no narrowings.\n\n**Witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/NRS_484D/NRS_484D_165_4.lean`): each trace has 31 scenes, 10 s apart, from 0 to 300 s. Every witness is judged only over 200–300 s, so the 180 s look-back for \"parked\" never runs past the start of the trace.\n\n| Witness | Scene | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|\n| forbid | car at rest, high beam | violated |\n| permit | car at rest, low beam | compliant |\n| idle | car at rest, headlamps off | not applicable |\n| blind | car at rest, headlamp state not observed | unknown |\n| branch_1 | car drives at 10 m/s until 270 s, then stops with high beam: too short a halt to count as parked | not applicable |\n| branch_2 (added) | a bicycle at rest with high beam: not in the vehicle aggregate | not applicable |\n\nI added branch_2 so that some witness tests the vehicle-class condition.\n\nOne read-only search of the Core files was blocked because it needed approval and this session can't grant it. I didn't need it, since the provided surface covered everything. The run log and these notes are in `task_result.md` in the working directory.",
